      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Founded in 1898, the village incorporated as Prospect Heights before renaming itself Peoria Heights in 1901 to avoid confusion with Chicago’s Prospect Heights.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        12,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peoria_Heights%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The village’s red water tower, accessible by elevator, crowns Tower Park and offers three observation decks overlooking Peoria, Tazewell, and Woodford counties.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peoria_Heights%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Forest Park Nature Center on the bluff preserves a native prairie and hosts miles of trails for hikers of all skill levels.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peoria_Heights%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Peoria Heights marked its 100th anniversary in 1998 with community celebrations and historical reflections.",
